    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, the exhaustion part is real. but the harder part is that i don't know where to take him. everything i write for him just feels like he's stuck in this loop of suffering but nothing changes. it feels dishonest to give him some big \"hopeful\" ending where he suddenly realizes life is worth it, because that doesn't feel real. it feels like he's just waiting for the end, and honestly, i'm struggling to see the point in writing a story where he just keeps struggling for no reason. what's the point of a character just existing in pain if there's no resolution?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
